# Per-agent engagement configs. RETIRED as a concept (CLAUDE.md §4 item 42:
# engagement belongs to the organisation now, as org/engagement.json), but
# ignored rather than merely absent for two reasons: a scaffold created
# before that phase can still have one on disk, and this file is what makes
# CLAUDE.md's long-standing "gitignored, never committed" claim about them
# actually TRUE — until now nothing enforced it, so a single `git add -A`
# would have put a real client's scope into history permanently (§5, "Git
# hygiene"). The tracked example for the CURRENT shape is
# shared/engagement.example.json; there is deliberately no committed
# example of this retired per-agent one any more.
engagement_config.py
engagement_config_lab.py

# Local dev tooling for driving the live GUI with a real browser
# (Playwright MCP registration) — machine-specific paths, not product code.
.mcp.json
playwright-mcp-config.json

# Operator workflow notes (Claude Code memory — not product docs)
MEMORY.md
UX_LAWS_AUDIT.md

# Build history (operator-internal; box-specific values, published from a fresh repo)
docs/history/

# Built packages (packaging/build-deb.sh, build-runtime.sh)
dist/

# Local Claude Code permissions: per-developer, never published.
.claude/settings.json
